# Copy to .env and fill in real values. .env is already gitignored (see
# .gitignore) — never commit it.
#
# These are read directly by the gateway process via os.Getenv at
# startup (cmd/gateway/main.go's buildPipeline) — one per configured
# deployment's api_key_env field in config.yaml (access_key_id_env /
# secret_access_key_env / session_token_env for a bedrock deployment).
# A deployment that sets the *_file sibling instead (api_key_file, ...)
# bypasses the environment entirely — the value is read from that file,
# re-read periodically by dataplane.Pipeline.RunCredentialReloadLoop,
# and its *_env variable is never consulted; see
# docs/how-to/rotate-credentials.md. The names below match
# gateway/config.example.yaml's openai and anthropic deployments; its
# gemini and bedrock deployments name GEMINI_API_KEY and
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY (optional AWS_SESSION_TOKEN).
# Add or rename entries here to match whatever deployments your own
# config.yaml actually declares.
#
# Everything else gateway reads (Redis addresses, budget persistence
# path, guardrail policy version, ...) is YAML config — the config file
# path is the -config flag — not an environment variable, except where
# config.yaml names one under another *_env key (admin.token_env and its
# viewer/cost_viewer/operator siblings, redis_password_env in each Redis
# block, config_propagation.signing_secret_env, alerting.webhook_url_env
# / signing_secret_env, the guardrails bedrock_guardrails / embed_sim
# *_env fields); those are os.Getenv reads too and belong here when
# your config sets them. The gateway's own code reads no other variable
# by NAME; the Go runtime and libraries it links do — notably
# AUTOMEMLIMIT (the cgroup GOMEMLIMIT probe; AUTOMEMLIMIT=off skips it,
# see README.md), the OpenTelemetry SDK's own OTEL_* (any
# telemetry.exporter other than "none"; its OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_* only
# under "otlp"; docker-compose.yml sets OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_INSECURE=true)
# and net/http's HTTP_PROXY / HTTPS_PROXY / NO_PROXY on every upstream
# client — see docs/operations/DEPLOY.md's Configuration Reference
# section.

OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
